PTX MP-self+texture-after-generic-read
"One thread stores 1 to y, loads it back (reads 1), then loads y through the texture proxy. The texture load may read the initial 0: the store and the texture load are in different proxies with no proxy fence between them (8.6). The generic load before it changes nothing: a generic read is ordered before a later write of the same address in any proxy (D49), not before a later read: allowed."
{
y=0;
P0:r0=0;
P0:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0       ;
 st.relaxed.cta y, 1 ;
 ld.weak r0, y       ;
 tld.weak r1, y      ;
exists
(P0:r0 == 1 /\ P0:r1 == 0)
